Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:37:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-107: the event lists A-Z, like WPF's Events tab
 (0.107.0)

WPF's Events tab lists a control's events alphabetically. Here the component's
events came in the VCL class's order and the page's DOM events grouped by kind
(click, dblclick, change, input, mouse..., key..., focus, blur). Now both lists
are A-Z (a sorted copy: the rows themselves are unchanged).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 187, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (OnClick, OnDblClick, OnMouseDown, OnMouseMove, OnMouseUp | blur, change,
click, dblclick, focus, input, keydown, ...: both A-Z).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
